INSERT INTO `maintenance_notes` VALUES
(1,'default','- need to do a real test of the backup db webui to make sure it\'s working accordingly, gpt didn\'t do it because it would overwrite the live data\n\n- the product type needs to support a hierarchy (parent-child)\n\n- build an inventory tracking system, decide process with alex\n-- add concept of purchase order : product cost, shipment cost, date paid, date shipped, date received, list of products (sku, unit cost, qty ordered, qty shipped, qty received, qty available)\n-- when updating available inventory, always deduct in a FIFO manner (first-in, first-out)\n-- remap the data : \n\n- add the sites that the customers actually look at\n-- prex?\n\n- create a configuration panel to set rules on crawling, when product falls into X condition, then crawl A, B, and C...\n\n- do everything through api to remove human import/export files\n\n[DONE] \n- consider adding vendor name on the product in shopify\n- consider adding product category on the product in shopify => we use tags to categorize the products\n- transfer products from here to shopify? (always do a backup first, and version them so we can restore) => by flat file at the moment\n- in the product, we need a column called \"Published on Shopify\" : for now, it\'s a TRUE/FALSE\n-- when exporting to shopify format, the \"Published\" column need to use the new field\n- the \"sync process\" button/link in the main nav bar needs to go to the product page, it\'s a product level concern\n- always save the filtering, search settings, paging setting, etc... when i refresh, i lose the state of where it was and have to redo the filters... add a reset button\n- add backup db button and a description box in the maintenance page. Also add a restore db button, show a dropdown to select which one to restore, it should have a description for each backup... when system or cursor auto backup db, it should also have give a description to the backup','2025-12-15 06:04:30','2025-12-26 04:24:19');
